{
  "_readme": [
    "The ladders, the leaguestart lists and the player levers. Hand-edited; nothing",
    "generates this file.",
    "",
    "A ladder is one row per tier, richest first. `cut` is in DIVINE ORBS, never chaos —",
    "chaos drifts against everything real over a league and a ladder written in it",
    "re-tiers the whole game as the league goes on. `cut: null` means the rung is not won",
    "on price at all: bases T0 is a quality condition, currency T4 is the player's click",
    "floor, currency T5/T6 are the leaguestart lists below, and gems T5 is a quality gate.",
    "",
    "`persistent` is the answer to a click floor set higher than a tier cut. On league",
    "start a divine is 60c, so a 5c floor erases T3 at 3c — a persistent tier is never",
    "",
    "`clickFloor: true` is the rung the player's own min-click value defines, and currency",
    "and gems each have one at T4. It is not the same as `cut: null` — a null cut means the",
    "rung is won some other way entirely (a quality gate, a name list), while this one is won",
    "by clearing the floor. Without the distinction T4 is unreachable and everything between",
    "the floor and T3 falls through to hidden.",
    "hidden by any ground-floor rule, whatever the player set.",
    "",
    "The style fields name templates, sounds and sizes defined in buckets/buckets.md.",
    "`icon` overrides the template's own icon; null keeps it. `beam` is always permanent —",
    "the docs have no temporary beam anywhere. `sound: null` is silence.",
    "",
    "`default` is not in any doc. It is today's ladder, kept verbatim for the two families",
    "buckets/ does not cover yet — misc and replicas — so they classify exactly as they",
    "did before this file existed. Delete it when they get docs of their own.",
    "",
    "The map rows carry a tier each, and the tiers are distinct on purpose. A map treatment",
    "is not won on price and the numbers mean nothing as a ladder — but a block says which",
    "style it wants through the tier in its `#@` note, and three treatments sharing a tier",
    "would be three blocks the styler cannot tell apart. So they are numbered loudest first.",
    "",
    "The unique ladder has ONE cut per tier, not a take/check pair. `take` is the guaranteed",
    "value — the cheapest unique on the base — and `check` is the aspirational one, the",
    "dearest. Both are read against the same cuts. Land on the same rung and it is a take;",
    "land on different rungs and the bucket takes the louder one as a check. T4 has no cut",
    "because it is the catch-all: a priced unique base never hides.",
    "",
    "`unit` says what a cut is denominated in. Divine is the default and is right for a market",
    "ladder; the unique cuts are in chaos because they are a floor on attention, and hovering",
    "does not get more expensive because divine went up.",
    "",
    "`check` is the marker a Check verb lays over the tier it sits on, and gold is its colour",
    "code. It replaces the border, the size and the minimap icon outright, and RECOLOURS the",
    "beam rather than adding one — a rung with no beam stays without, because a maybe should",
    "not be more findable on the ground than the guaranteed drops around it. Sound is never",
    "touched. Change `beam` and `icon.colour` together or the two marks disagree; both take one",
    "of the eleven names the game allows, while `border` is RGBA because a label colour is not",
    "limited to those.",
    "",
    "`tint` is the background, and it is a BLEND rather than a colour: the rung's own",
    "background mixed `strength` of the way toward `colour`, so every rung stays recognisably",
    "itself and turns gold-ward. At 0 a check looks exactly like its tier; at 1 every rung",
    "collapses onto the same gold. The text is not configured at all — it is black or white,",
    "whichever reads on the blend that comes out.",
    "",
    "`neverHidden` names the currency the click floor may not take away. They keep whatever",
    "styling their own rung gives them - this is not a promotion - but the floor cannot drop",
    "them below it. Scarabs are matched by name because the exchange spreads them across two",
    "groups, 124 under Fragments and 2 under Currency; allflames have a group of their own."
  ],
